        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5af21dc5-ff79-5955-9221-e10631a8374f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ernie Hine, Arthur Chandler, Arthur Lochhead, Johnny Duncan, Jamie Vardy\n- Organizations: Manchester United F.C., Leicester City F.C., Barnsley, Huddersfield Town, England national team, The Wednesday\n- Places: Old Trafford, Greater Manchester, England\n- Concepts: professional football, striker, Premier League, First Division\n\nFacts:\n- Manchester United Football Club was founded as Newton Heath LYR Football Club in 1878.\n- Manchester United Football Club changed its name to Manchester United in 1902.\n- Manchester United Football Club moved to Old Trafford in 1910.\n- Ernest William \"Ernie\" Hine was born on 9 April 1901 and died on 15 April 1974.\n- Ernie Hine was a professional footballer who played for Barnsley, Leicester City, Huddersfield Town, and Manchester United.\n- In the 1928–29 season, Leicester City finished runners-up in the First Division, one point behind The Wednesday.\n- In the 1928–29 season, Leicester City was led by Ernie Hine, Arthur Chandler, Arthur Lochhead, and captain Johnny Duncan.\n- Ernie Hine, Arthur Chandler, and Arthur Lochhead remain among Leicester City's top five all-time goalscorers.\n- Jamie Richard Vardy was born on 11 January 1987.\n- Jamie Vardy is an English professional footballer who plays as a striker for Leicester City and the England national team.\n- Manchester United Football Club is based in Old Trafford, Greater Manchester, England, and competes in the Premier League.\n- Manchester United Football Club is nicknamed \"the Red Devils.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fc46d8b0-f1ad-5679-b24d-1e689ece2d05",
        "text": "Page: Ernie Hine. Sentence: Ernest William \"Ernie\" Hine (9 April 1901 – 15 April 1974) was a professional footballer who played for Barnsley, Leicester City, Huddersfield Town and Manchester United.\nPage: Manchester United F.C.. Sentence: Manchester United Football Club is a professional football club based in Old Trafford, Greater Manchester, England, that competes in the Premier League, the top flight of English football.\nPage: Manchester United F.C.. Sentence: Nicknamed \"the Red Devils\", the club was founded as Newton Heath LYR Football Club in 1878, changed its name to Manchester United in 1902 and moved to its current stadium, Old Trafford, in 1910.\nPage: 1928–29 Leicester City F.C. season. Sentence: Led by their formidable strike force of Ernie Hine, Arthur Chandler and Arthur Lochhead (all three of whom are still placed today among Leicester's top five goalscorers of all-time) and inspirational captain and creative lynch-pin Johnny Duncan, Leicester finished runners-up in the First Division, just one point behind winners The Wednesday.\nPage: Jamie Vardy. Sentence: Jamie Richard Vardy (\"né\" Gill; born 11 January 1987) is an English professional footballer who plays as a striker for Premier League club Leicester City and the England national team.",
